  "id": "nativism",
  "term": "nativism",
  "definition": "Nativism is the view that, in whatever area it is applied, some feature or capacity is inborn rather than acquired. In this historical usage, it can refer to claims about innate knowledge or intuition, native forms of space and time, or inborn biological characters.",
